# Screens for the InitechDOS 3.30 User's Guide (1024-3300-11), bead initech-ipu5.7.
# name|serial marker[#count]|keystrokes (printf %b; \n = Enter, \\ = backslash)
# The marker is text of the LAST command's output; #count is how many times it
# has appeared on the serial mirror (typed keys echo there too) when the
# screen is complete.  Regenerate with `make pubs-screens`; `make
# test-pubs-screens` re-captures every screen and diffs it against the book.
startup|SHELL-READY|
errors|Required parameter missing|CLS\nB:\nDIRECTORY\nTYPE\n
dir|bytes free|CLS\nDIR\n
type|Copies of the cover sheet|CLS\nTYPE MEMO.TXT\n
copy|bytes free|CLS\nCOPY MEMO.TXT MEMO.BAK\nDIR\n
del|File not found|COPY MEMO.TXT MEMO.BAK\nCLS\nDEL MEMO.BAK\nTYPE MEMO.BAK\n
paths|bytes free|CLS\nMD REPORTS\nCOPY MEMO.TXT REPORTS\nCD REPORTS\nDIR\n
ren|bytes free|CLS\nREN MEMO.TXT MEMO.OLD\nDIR\n
wild|A:\PHONE.TXT|CLS\nATTRIB *.TXT\n
cdsub|bytes free|CLS\nCD SAMPLES\nCD\nCD ..\nCD\nCD SAMPLES\nDIR\n
tree|None#2|CLS\nTREE\n
vol|Volume in drive A is INITECH|CLS\nVOL\n
label|Volume in drive A is WORKDISK|CLS\nLABEL\nWORKDISK\nVOL\n
chkdsk|bytes free|CLS\nCHKDSK\n
backup|bytes free|CLS\nXCOPY *.TXT BACKUP\\\nCD BACKUP\nDIR\n
autoexec|PATH=A:\APPS#2|CLS\nTYPE AUTOEXEC.BAT\nSET\n
greet|Your report is due Friday.|CLS\nCD SAMPLES\nTYPE GREET.BAT\nGREET Peter Friday\n
check|cannot be found.#2|CLS\nCD SAMPLES\nTYPE CHECK.BAT\nCHECK GREET.BAT\nCHECK NOFILE.TXT\n
cover|The cover sheets are ready.|CLS\nCD SAMPLES\nCOVER\n 
set|DEPT=PUBS#2|CLS\nSET DEPT=PUBS\nSET\n
prompt|A:\>#3|CLS\nPROMPT $N$G\nPROMPT\n
redir|Second line#2|CLS\nVER > LIST.TXT\nECHO Second line >> LIST.TXT\nTYPE LIST.TXT\n
stdin|Volume in drive A is REPORTS|CLS\nECHO REPORTS > NAME.TXT\nLABEL < NAME.TXT\nVOL\n
attrib|Access denied|CLS\nATTRIB +R PHONE.TXT\nATTRIB PHONE.TXT\nDEL PHONE.TXT\n
xcopys|File(s) copied|CLS\nXCOPY SAMPLES SAVED /S\nD

